 "result_text": "I didn't remove the authentication requirement. I improved the error message instead, which the issue offered as the fallback. I only checked that `git_machete.github` still imports. I didn't run the tests or try a real `create-pr`.\n\nReading public repos works without a token, which is why the URL opens in a browser. `create-pr` sends a `POST` to `/pulls`, and GitHub needs a token for that. When the request has no token, GitHub answers a `POST` to `/pulls` with `404` instead of `401`/`403`. That `404` is what produced the \"not found \u2026 (expired token?)\" message.\n\nThe `404` handler in `git_machete/github.py` now words the error differently depending on whether a token was sent:\n- **No token:** the message says the endpoint doesn't exist or needs authentication, and that creating a PR needs a token even on a public repo. It also lists where to set a token and links to `https://github.com/settings/tokens`.\n- **Token present:** the message says the endpoint may not exist, or the token may be expired or lack `repo` access.",
